<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS - Qantas says union agreement close.</title>
<headline>RTRS - Qantas says union agreement close.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Qantas Airways Ltd said on Wednesday it was close to reaching an enterprise bargaining agreement with various unions.</p>
<p>The airline said it finalised a framework agreement with the peak union body, the ACTU, while the transport workers had voted overwhelmingly in favour of the agreement. Four other unions, which includes flight attendants and metalworkers, had agreed in principle and would seek the support of their membership.</p>
<p>Agreements with three other unions with small memberships were still to be finalised. Qantas is 25 percent owned by British Airways Plc. -- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
